{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794761891,"nonce":"WC9hTVKj3NZHKnuy5Uz441TvjVg=","title":"A full paint of the cn demo costs 9 ms, and half of it was adding up ancestors and hashing","message":"Measured in a headless session of the real cn demo (900 x 900, paint only, no read-back; tools/blinc-bench example cn_demo_costs with COSTS_ONLY_PAINT=\u003cframes\u003e), release build, median of 1,500 to 2,500 frames: 9.2 ms. In the owner's window the same frames (not served from the cache) measured 10 to 17 ms in the render phase, against 0.45 ms for a frame served from the cache (BLINC_MOTION_TRACE over 84 s of use: 1,120 full paints, 723 cache frames).\n\nWhere it went, from a sampling profile with symbols: `subtree_paints_over` (canvas_order.rs) recursed through a subtree and called `RenderTree::get_absolute_bounds` for every node, which walks every ancestor, allocates a Vec and hashes a scroll lookup per level; it was about half of the busy time. The `render_nodes` map used the standard SipHash, about 20% in hashing between it and the scroll maps.\n\nChanges: the walk carries the parent's absolute bounds down to each child (a node's bounds are its parent's, its offset in the parent and the parent's scroll), with a test that equals the ancestor sum under nested scrolled containers; `render_nodes` uses `rustc_hash::FxBuildHasher`. 9.2 ms to 6.0 ms with the first, 4.8 ms with both.\n\nLeft in the profile, in order: `cull::draws_outside` and `plan_cross_stream_groups::visit` recurse through the tree and call `get_absolute_bounds` and `ancestors` again; `LayoutTree::get_absolute_bounds` itself at 8.7% self; the scroll and binding maps still hash with SipHash; allocation churn from `ancestors()` returning a Vec. `ElementRegistry::get_element_type`, `compound_matches` and `apply_stylesheet_layout_overrides` are the cost of a relayout (about 12 ms in cn_profile, 3,100 of 4,700 busy samples), which the window rarely pays (style phase 24 us median in the trace).\n\nNot changed: which frames are full paints at all. Hover over the page gave about 120 full paints in two seconds in the trace with no redraw signal asking.\n\nLabels: perf, area:layout.","files":null}]}